<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tsolo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tsolo is a small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-cape">Eastern Cape</a> province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsitsa-river">Tsitsa River</a> north of Mthatha. It lies in the former heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpondomise">Mpondomise</a> kingdom and became a magistracy after Cape annexation. During apartheid it formed part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transkei">Transkei</a> bantustan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tsolo.jpg" alt="Tsolo" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Esteban 20017 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_panor%C3%A1mica_de_Tsolo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
